lane: feed-linear-view
why: profiled on the FASTEST channel path (90.4us), 54% of the time is
  runFree -- the interpreter's dispatch loop -- against 5% in the
  channel's own feed and 12% in boxed ChunkBuf writes. The cause is in
  `feed`/`feedBatched`: per element they do
      async(St.uncons(x).runWith).flatMap { ... }
  which BUILDS a Free program, INTERPRETS it, wraps the answer in
  Async.Run, and has that interpreted again by the outer runFree. Two
  interpreter passes per element to take the head of a list.
how: `Stream` already declares `iterator` as "the linear view ... an
  instance may specialize it to skip the per-element Option and tuple
  of uncons" -- the mechanism exists and the feed does not use it.
  Feeding a channel IS a linear consume-once walk, so:
    - override `iterator` on the pure collection instances (LazyList,
      List) to hand back the collection's own iterator;
    - have feed/feedBatched pull from St.iterator instead of
      recursing through uncons.
  Equivalent by construction: the default iterator IS
  uncons(_).runWith, the same call with the same handler, so an
  effectful source behaves exactly as before.
land only if measured faster on okayChannelForeach_chunkNative and the
  matrix is unchanged; the risk is a source whose iterator and uncons
  disagree, which the laws must catch.
